  "id": "low-pass-filter",
  "term": "low-pass filter",
  "definition": "A low-pass filter is something that reduces higher-frequency parts of a sound while letting lower-frequency parts pass through more easily. In this context, face masks were described as acting like a low-pass filter because they dampen higher-frequency speech sounds.",
